,"gloss":"Elonbeth-hanan","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":3},{"base":"H1125","lemma":"בֶּן־אֲבִינָדָב","tr":"ben-a·vi·na·dav","gloss":"Ben-Abinadab","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":2},{"base":"H1127","lemma":"בֶּן־גֶּ֫בֶר","tr":"ben-ge·ver","gloss":"Ben-Geber","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":2},{"base":"H1128","lemma":"בֶּן־דֶּ֫קֶר","tr":"ben-de·qer","gloss":"Ben-deker","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":2},{"base":"H1133","lemma":"בֶּן־חוּר","tr":"ben-chur","gloss":"Ben-hur","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":2},{"base":"H1195","lemma":"בַּעֲנָא","tr":"ba·a·na","gloss":"Baana","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":3},{"base":"H0065","lemma":"אָבֵל מְחוֹלָה","tr":"a·vel me·cho·lah","gloss":"Abel-meholah","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":6},{"base":"H1568","lemma":"גִּלְעָד","tr":"gil·ad","gloss":"Gilead","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":134},{"base":"H8010","lemma":"שְׁלֹמֹה","tr":"she·lo·moh","gloss":"Solomon","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":293}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"NUM","chapter":32,"verse":41,"verseEnd":41,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Jair, a descendant of Manasseh, went and captured their villages and called them Havvoth-jair.","from":13},{"book":"DEU","chapter":3,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"At that time we captured all sixty of his cities. There was not a single city we failed to take—the entire region of Argob, the kingdom of Og in Bashan.","from":13},{"book":"JOS","chapter":17,"verse":11,"verseEnd":11,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Within Issachar and Asher, Manasseh was assigned Beth-shean, Ibleam, Dor (that is, Naphath), Endor, Taanach, and Megiddo, each with their surrounding settlements.","from":12},{"book":"1KI","chapter":1,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"But Zadok the priest, Benaiah son of Jehoiada, Nathan the prophet, Shimei, Rei, and Davidʼs mighty men would not join Adonijah.","from":18},{"book":"GEN","chapter":32,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"When Jacob saw them, he said, “This is the camp of God.” So he named that place Mahanaim.","from":14},{"book":"NUM","chapter":21,"verse":21,"verseEnd":35,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Then Israel sent messengers to Sihon king of the Amorites, saying, “Let us pass through your land. We will not turn aside into any field or vineyard, or drink water from any well. We will stay on the Kingʼs Highway until we have passed through your territory.” But Sihon would not let Israel pass through his territory. Instead, he gathered his whole army and went out to confront Israel in the wilderness. When he came to Jahaz, he fought against Israel. And Israel put him to the sword and took possession of his land, from the Arnon to the Jabbok—but only up to the border of the Ammonites, because it was fortified. Israel captured all the cities of the Amorites and occupied them, including Heshbon and all its villages.","from":19},{"book":"DEU","chapter":2,"verse":26,"verseEnd":37,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"So from the Wilderness of Kedemoth I sent messengers with an offer of peace to Sihon king of Heshbon, saying, “Let us pass through your land; we will stay on the main road. We will not turn to the right or to the left. You can sell us food to eat and water to drink in exchange for silver. Only let us pass through on foot, just as the descendants of Esau who live in Seir and the Moabites who live in Ar did for us, until we cross the Jordan into the land that the LORD our God is giving us.” But Sihon king of Heshbon would not let us pass through, for the LORD your God had made his spirit stubborn and his heart obstinate, that He might deliver him into your hand, as is the case this day.","from":19},{"book":"DEU","chapter":3,"verse":1,"verseEnd":17,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Then we turned and went up the road to Bashan, and Og king of Bashan and his whole army came out to meet us in battle at Edrei. But the LORD said to me, “Do not fear him, for I have delivered him into your hand, along with all his people and his land. Do to him as you did to Sihon king of the Amorites, who lived in Heshbon.” So the LORD our God also delivered Og king of Bashan and his whole army into our hands. We struck them down until no survivor was left. At that time we captured all sixty of his cities. There was not a single city we failed to take—the entire region of Argob, the kingdom of Og in Bashan. All these cities were fortified with high walls and gates and bars, and there were many more unwalled villages.","from":19}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":5},{"id":"kings-prophets","title":"Kings, prophets and the house of David","people":2}]},"20-28":{"people":[{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":2,"firstVerse":20},{"id":"judah-h3063g","name":"Judah","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":2,"firstVerse":20},{"id":"solomon-h8010","name":"Solomon","kind":"person","brief":"King of Judah","count":5,"firstVerse":21}],"places":[{"id":"euphrates-h6578","name":"Euphrates","kind":"place","brief":"","count":2,"firstVerse":21},{"id":"egypt-h4714g","name":"Egypt","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":21},{"id":"philistia-h6429","name":"Philistia","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":21},{"id":"gaza-h5804","name":"Gaza","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":24},{"id":"tiphsah-h8607g","name":"Tiphsah","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":24},{"id":"beersheba-h0884","name":"Beersheba","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":25},{"id":"dan-h1835g","name":"Dan","kind":"place","brief":"In Dan","count":1,"firstVerse":25}],"words":[{"base":"H8010","lemma":"שְׁלֹמֹה","tr":"she·lo·moh","gloss":"Solomon","lang":"h","inPassage":7,"uses":293},{"base":"H5676","lemma":"עֵ֫בֶר","tr":"e·ver","gloss":"side: beside","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":90},{"base":"H5104","lemma":"נָהָר","tr":"na·har","gloss":"River","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":119},{"base":"H3734","lemma":"כֹּר","tr":"kor","gloss":"kor","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":9},{"base":"H0884","lemma":"בְּאֵר שֶׁ֫בַע","tr":"be·er she·va","gloss":"Beersheba","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":68},{"base":"H5483","lemma":"סוּס","tr":"sus","gloss":"swallow","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":140},{"base":"H1241","lemma":"בָּקָר","tr":"ba·qar","gloss":"cattle","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":183},{"base":"H0075","lemma":"אָבַס","tr":"a·vas","gloss":"to fatten","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"H3180","lemma":"יַחְמוּר","tr":"yach·mur","gloss":"roebuck","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"H8607","lemma":"תִּפְסַח","tr":"tiph·sach","gloss":"Tiphsah","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":2}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"GEN","chapter":15,"verse":18,"verseEnd":18,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"On that day the Lordmade a covenant with Abram, saying, “To your descendants I have given this land—from the river of Egypt to the great River Euphrates—","from":21},{"book":"MIC","chapter":4,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"And each man will sit under his own vine and under his own fig tree, with no one to frighten him. For the mouth of the LORD of Hosts has spoken.","from":25},{"book":"JOS","chapter":1,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"Your territory shall extend from the wilderness and Lebanon to the great River Euphrates—all the land of the Hittites—and west as far as the Great Sea.","from":21},{"book":"1CH","chapter":22,"verse":9,"verseEnd":9,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"But a son will be born to you who will be a man of rest. I will give him rest from all his enemies on every side; for his name will be Solomon, and I will grant to Israel peace and quiet during his reign.","from":24},{"book":"GEN","chapter":22,"verse":17,"verseEnd":17,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"I will surely bless you, and I will multiply your descendants like the stars in the sky and the sand on the seashore. Your descendants will possess the gates of their enemies.","from":20},{"book":"1KI","chapter":3,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Your servant is here among the people You have chosen, a people too numerous to count or number.","from":20},{"book":"2CH","chapter":1,"verse":14,"verseEnd":14,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Solomon accumulated 1,400 chariots and 12,000 horses, which he stationed in the chariot cities and also with him in Jerusalem.","from":26},{"book":"ZEC","chapter":3,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"On that day, declares the LORD of Hosts, you will each invite your neighbor to sit under your own vine and fig tree.’”","from":25}],"notes":[{"id":"land-promise-fulfilled","title":"The land promised and the land possessed","kind":"prophecy"}],"groups":[{"id":"royal-line","title":"The royal line: Judah to David to Jesus","people":2},{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":2}]},"29-34":{"people":[{"id":"solomon-h8010","name":"Solomon","kind":"person","brief":"King of Judah","count":3,"firstVerse":29},{"id":"calcol-h3633g","name":"Calcol","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Mahol","count":1,"firstVerse":31},{"id":"darda-h1862","name":"Darda","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Mahol","count":1,"firstVerse":31},{"id":"ethan-h0387g","name":"Ethan","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Mahol","count":1,"firstVerse":31},{"id":"heman-h1968g","name":"Heman","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Mahol","count":1,"firstVerse":31},{"id":"mahol-h4235","name":"Mahol","kind":"person","brief":"Father of Ethan","count":1,"firstVerse":31},{"id":"zerah-h2226i","name":"Zerah","kind":"person","brief":"Judah's son","count":1,"firstVerse":31}],"places":[{"id":"egypt-h4714g","name":"Egypt","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":30},{"id":"lebanon-h3844g","name":"Lebanon","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":33}],"words":[{"base":"H2451","lemma":"חׇכְמָה","tr":"chokh·mah","gloss":"wisdom","lang":"h","inPassage":6,"uses":153},{"base":"H8010","lemma":"שְׁלֹמֹה","tr":"she·lo·moh","gloss":"Solomon","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":293},{"base":"H1696","lemma":"דָבַר","tr":"da·var","gloss":"to speak: speak","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":1142},{"base":"H7235","lemma":"רָבָה","tr":"ra·vah","gloss":"to multiply","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":227},{"base":"H3633","lemma":"כַּלְכֹּל","tr":"kal·kol","gloss":"Calcol","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"H0250","lemma":"אֶזְרָחִי","tr":"ez·ra·chi","gloss":"Ezrahite","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":3},{"base":"H0505","lemma":"אֶ֫לֶף","tr":"e·leph","gloss":"thousand","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":506},{"base":"H0387","lemma":"אֵיתָן","tr":"e·tan","gloss":"Ethan","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":8},{"base":"H0231","lemma":"אֵזוֹב","tr":"e·zov","gloss":"hyssop","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":10},{"base":"H1968","lemma":"הֵימָן","tr":"he·man","gloss":"Heman","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":17}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"1KI","chapter":3,"verse":12,"verseEnd":12,"votes":10,"source":"both","text":"behold, I will do what you have asked. I will give you a wise and discerning heart, so that there will never have been another like you, nor will ever be.","from":29},{"book":"JAS","chapter":3,"verse":17,"verseEnd":17,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"But the wisdom from above is first of all pure, then peace-loving, gentle, accommodating, full of mercy and good fruit, impartial, and sincere.","from":29},{"book":"JAS","chapter":1,"verse":5,"verseEnd":5,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"Now if any of you lacks wisdom, he should ask God, who gives generously to all without finding fault, and it will be given to him.","from":29},{"book":"GEN","chapter":25,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"But while he was still alive, Abraham gave gifts to the sons of his concubines and sent them away from his son Isaac to the land of the east.","from":30},{"book":"1KI","chapter":4,"verse":20,"verseEnd":20,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"The people of Judah and Israel were as numerous as the sand on the seashore, and they were eating and drinking and rejoicing.","from":29},{"book":"1CH","chapter":2,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"The sons of Zerah: Zimri, Ethan, Heman, Calcol, and Dara—five in all.","from":31},{"book":"1CH","chapter":15,"verse":19,"verseEnd":19,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"The musicians Heman, Asaph, and Ethan were to sound the bronze cymbals.","from":31},{"book":"2CH","chapter":9,"verse":23,"verseEnd":23,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"All the kings of the earth sought an audience with Solomon to hear the wisdom that God had put in his heart.","from":34}],"notes":[],"groups":[]}}